        "math_academy_id": "q-275612",
        "problem": "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-4y+3x=8 \\\\ 2x=-3,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $8$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $8$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n.",
        "worked_solution": "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=8 \\\\ 2x+0y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
